From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Garcia <lex@ibm.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:51:35 -0500
Subject: agent host: restore the codex agent without its copilot proxy

`CodexAgent` supports an `openai` usage source alongside the Copilot-CAPI one, so it is pinned to that and runs `codex` on the user's own OpenAI credentials. The Copilot-CAPI model catalogue, the proxy handle threaded through the app-server connection and the sign-out fallback to Copilot go with the proxy; models come from the app-server's own `model/list`. `@openai/codex` returns as a devDependency, and registration stays upstream's register-on-enable so codex is off unless `chat.agentHost.codexAgent.enabled` is set.

